homelab-pgbouncer (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the 0.1.1 "verify port is listening, escalate to restart"
    check was unreliable -- a stale bind on the WRONG address still
    shows the port as listening, so it never actually escalated (caught
    live: stayed on 127.0.0.1 despite listen_addr=* after a fresh
    install). Restart decisions are now based on comparing the
    previous vs. new listen_addr/listen_port values directly (restart
    only when either changed, or on first activation) rather than
    inspecting `ss` output.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:40:00 -0500

homelab-pgbouncer (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: `systemctl reload pgbouncer` (SIGHUP) does not rebind
    listen_addr/listen_port -- confirmed empirically that a fresh
    install stayed bound to the vendor's stock pgbouncer.ini default
    (listen_addr=localhost) even after our config was written and
    reloaded, since pgbouncer itself had already started with the old
    config before this package's postinst ran. Now verifies the
    configured port is actually listening after reload and escalates to
    a full restart if not, matching the same pattern already used for
    HAProxy in homelab-mail-proxy.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:30:00 -0500

homelab-pgbouncer (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Phase 2 of the cross-package Postgres role
    strategy: configures PgBouncer (scram-sha-256, static userlist.txt)
    in front of homelab-database's shared `homelab` database, via a
    drop-in file activated through pgbouncer's native %include
    directive. Ships scripts/bootstrap-pgbouncer-entry.sh for other
    packages' installers to register a role's SCRAM secret without a
    stored/network admin credential (local, SSH-remote, or manual
    fallback -- same tiering as homelab-database's
    bootstrap-app-role.sh).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:00:00 -0500
